// **Two imported generators both declaring `csv_column`**, which has to be refused: a generator
// cannot qualify its own attributes -- `#[csv.column]` is not a shape the grammar has -- so the
// collision belongs to whoever imported both, and the only resolution is to stop.
//
// It is reported at the **second import**, which is the line to delete, and names the attribute
// and one of the two claimants.
use derive_csv
use derive_tsv

#[derive(Csv)]
struct Customer {
    #[csv_column(name: "ID")]
    id: int
}

fn main() {
    print(customer_csv_header())
}
